{#
    Video Commerce  products flagged in the dashboard's Video Commerce section.

    The clips are NOT typed into the customizer. The merchant enables Video
    Commerce on a product in the dashboard and uploads the clip there. The
    endpoint GET /storefront/videoCommerceProducts returns exactly those
    products. app.js fetches them and builds one <custom-falak-product-card>
    per product inside [data-vc-grid] the same card every other section uses,
    which already prefers a product's clip over its still image.

    That endpoint is gated on the shop setting `enable_video_commerce`; when
    Video Commerce is off it answers 404 and app.js hides the whole section
    rather than leaving an empty headed band.

    The section starts `hidden` so it is invisible until the fetch completes
    (or fails). Shimmer tiles fill the grid while the fetch is in flight: their
    count matches `limit` so the page height does not jump on load.

    | component.title       | ?string | section heading, localized                     |
    | component.subtitle    | ?string | sub-heading under the title                    |
    | component.limit       | ?int    | max products to show (default 4)               |
    | component.columns     | ?string | cards per row on large screens (default "4")   |
    | component.badge_text  | ?string | pill overlaid on each clip (empty = hidden)    |
    | component.show_badge  | ?bool   | master toggle for the badge pill               |
    | component.playback    | ?string | "inview" or "hover" (default "inview")         |
    | component.show_actions| ?bool   | cart + wishlist buttons under each clip        |
    | position              | int     |                                                |

    Customizer bindings:
    | Element          | Tag                       |
    | h2.block__title  | data-falak-field="title"  |
    | p.block__subtitle| data-falak-field="subtitle"|

    NOTE: `show_badge|default(true)` fires on *empty* values, not only on
    undefined — so a merchant who switches the toggle off would get `true`
    back. The explicit "not defined" test below avoids that trap.
#}
{% set show_badge   = component.show_badge   is not defined or component.show_badge %}
{% set show_actions = component.show_actions is not defined or component.show_actions %}
{% set limit_count  = (component.limit|default(4) > 0) ? component.limit|default(4) : 4 %}

<section class="block block--video-commerce" id="video-commerce-{{ position }}"
         data-video-commerce
         data-limit="{{ limit_count }}"
         data-badge="{{ show_badge ? component.badge_text|default('') : '' }}"
         data-playback="{{ component.playback|default('inview') }}"
         data-actions="{{ show_actions ? '1' : '0' }}"
         hidden {{ falak_section() }}>
    <div class="container">

        <div class="block-vc__head" data-reveal="fade">
            {% if component.title %}
                <h2 class="block__title"
                    data-falak-field="title"
                    data-falak-label="{{ trans('editor.field.title') }}">{{ component.title }}</h2>
            {% endif %}
            {% if component.subtitle %}
                <p class="block__subtitle"
                   data-falak-field="subtitle"
                   data-falak-label="{{ trans('editor.field.description') }}">{{ component.subtitle }}</p>
            {% endif %}
        </div>

        {# Shimmer placeholders replaced by real cards once the fetch lands.
           Count matches `limit` so the grid keeps the right height while
           loading and nothing below it reflows. app.js clears them on success
           or hides the whole section on 404. #}
        <ul class="vc-grid"
            data-vc-grid
            style="--vc-columns: {{ component.columns|default('4') }}">
            {% for i in range(1, limit_count) %}
                <li class="vc-skeleton" aria-hidden="true"></li>
            {% endfor %}
        </ul>

    </div>
</section>
